<title>UK: Nestle UK to raise wholesale coffee price on June.</title>
<headline>Nestle UK to raise wholesale coffee price on June.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nestle UK Ltd, part of the Swiss food conglomerate Nestle SA, said on Wednesday it would raise its wholesale coffee price on Monday, June 2.</p>
<p>It takes about two or three weeks for the price to change on shop shelves. Typically, a 100 gramme jar in supermarkets will cost 10 pence more at around 1.99 stg, a company statement said.</p>
</text>
